{
  "schema": "icarus.dcm.vague-terms.v1",
  "description": "Reviewed values the deterministic resolver substitutes for vague operator words. The planner LLM may name a term (the planner grammar only offers these terms); only this file gives it a number. Every substitution is recorded as vague_term:<term> provenance and shown in the operator readback. Values are deliberately conservative and inside the Drone API contract bounds (takeoff <= 10 m, hold <= 60 s, orbit radius 3..15 m, yaw rate 5..60 deg/s). An unrecognised term falls back to family_defaults and is disclosed in the readback. Reviewed values only fill a missing or vague value: an explicit operator number inside the contract bounds is never replaced (visual_defaults.max_scan_step_deg bounds the reviewed step terms and defaults, not the operator), and any adjustment still needed for validity is shown on the readback line.",
